    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "`Publish` in `publish.go` writes to a temp file in the same folder as `dst`. It syncs that file to disk, then renames it over `dst`. If reading `src` fails, `dst` does not change and the temp file is deleted. The new file keeps the old file's permissions.\n\nI did not run the tests: `go test` needs your approval. I added `publish_test.go`. It checks that `dst` stays unchanged when a read fails partway.\n\nOpen issues:\n- If the process restarts during a copy, it leaves an orphan `.\u003cname\u003e.tmp-*` file. Customers never see it, but nothing deletes it.\n- On Windows, the rename fails if the web server opens `dst` without delete sharing. Most servers use delete sharing.",
